1. **SA-C re-run after SA-A AdjustQuantBlockAC fix lands** — does the
   raw_quant overlap rise from 49.6% to >90%? Does the err_c0 ratio
   collapse from 3× to ~1×? Does the Pass-2 sharpness convergence flip
   to byte-identity?
2. **Investigate why our `raw_quant` mode is q=5 not q=6** — is the
   buttloop scale-recomputation rounding direction different? Median/MAD
   threshold?
3. **Per-iter EPF sharpness instability probe** — dump sharpness at each
   buttloop iter (currently computed once outside the loop). If the W44-117
   seed wedge is real, it manifests as different sharpness on the final
   iter vs the seed iter.
